# FABLE-SONNET-OCC-ROOT-20260924-146: an own-field occurrence under a NAMED (method) root,
# `test\[N]field`, resolved by the same occurrence lookup the rootless `\[N]field` form uses
# (l2_own_find_occ) -- no second scanner.
#
# bafca4c (the author, 2026-09-28: assignment is not a declaration; an argument is its parameter): the two
# bare assignments of the argument `arg` declare nothing, and `test\[N]x` opens a place of declaration (book
# §11: «путь M\i снаружи открывает место объявления») -- arg has none, so test\[0]arg is refused where it
# stands, at the walked root ("no such occurrence").  (Q29 made them one cell, test\[0]arg = 2.)  Declared
# occurrences through a method root: unit_q24_repeated_decl.lm2.
fn: test (int: arg) int
    arg: 1
    arg: 2
    return: 0
end: test

int: got
got: test(0)
if: test\[0]arg != 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: test\arg != 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 83; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
